# Document Hierarchy Rules

## Required Files by Level

### Root Level (repo-root/)
```
README.md          # Project overview
AGENTS.md          # Agent guidance (always-applied rules)
DEV_STATE.md       # Cross-module state
docs/adr/          # Architecture decisions
tasks/             # Pending work queue
```

### Module Level (a2a-*/)
```
README.md          # Module purpose + quickstart
DEV_STATE.md       # Module-specific implementation state
```

### Feature Level (*/feature/)
```
README.md          # Feature docs
```

## DEV_STATE Protocol

**Always update before/after tasks:**

1. **Prune** — Remove completed items, duplicates
2. **Discover** — Scan for new work from code/sims/risks
3. **Write** — Add concrete testable tasks

### Content Rules

- Root: Cross-module facts only
- Each module: Own implementation details
- No abstract statements — all tasks testable
- Tasks >14 days → backlog with blocker reason

## Empty Queue Protocol

Empty backlog = **NOT** finished. Required actions:

1. Prune root + module DEV_STATE.md
2. Discover work (code, sims, risks, backlog)
3. Write tasks to DEV_STATE + tasks/pending/
4. Resume normal cycle

## Quick Reference Table

| Document | Purpose | Update When |
|----------|---------|-------------|
| AGENTS.md | Agent rules | Architecture changes |
| DEV_STATE.md | Current state | Before/after tasks |
| docs/adr/*.md | Decisions | New patterns |
| tasks/pending/*.md | Work queue | New tasks found |
| GLOSSARY.md | Terminology | New concepts |

## README Requirements

Every README must have:
- Purpose statement (1 sentence)
- Quickstart or link to one
- Key files/patterns section
